1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,833
Dear May Deer,

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,667
With a lovely family,

3
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,250
Dreaming of growing up each day.

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,167
Shy Chuan-Chuan Pangolin,

5
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,667
Quiet, with not a word to say,

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

7
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:20,083
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

8
00:00:20,583 --> 00:00:21,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

9
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,333
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

10
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:22,917
Don’t be shy!

11
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:23,917
Don’t be shy!

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Sing out loud!

13
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,833
Sing out loud!

14
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,417
Let your imagination shine!

15
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:31,167
Good friends in the forest,

16
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,083
Growing and playing together,

17
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:34,000
Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan!

18
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,333
ODEER MAYO / Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan

19
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,082
Being Uniquely You

20
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:44,000
We have gym class today.

21
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,833
We have gym class today.

22
00:00:45,833 --> 00:00:48,750
May, Chuan-Chuan, and the other children are warming up.

23
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:52,167
They’re getting ready to practice running.

24
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,167
Yay! We’re running today!

25
00:00:56,167 --> 00:00:59,500
I love running! Before I even get out of breath,

26
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,917
I’m whoosh! Across the finish line!

27
00:01:01,917 --> 00:01:04,833
I’m as fast as lightning! Haha!

28
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:07,083
Right, Chuan-Chuan?

29
00:01:07,083 --> 00:01:10,083
May, I’m so jealous of you.

30
00:01:10,083 --> 00:01:12,167
I-I don’t like running.

31
00:01:12,167 --> 00:01:15,917
I always get so tired and run so slowly.

32
00:01:16,583 --> 00:01:18,083
Chuan-Chuan, I’ll teach you a trick.

33
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:22,250
When you get tired, imagine a little choo-choo train running alongside you.

34
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:25,667
That way, you won’t feel so tired.

35
00:01:25,667 --> 00:01:25,917
Mm-hmm.

36
00:01:28,083 --> 00:01:30,083
Kids, today is gym class.

37
00:01:30,083 --> 00:01:32,583
Let’s see how fast you can run.

38
00:01:32,583 --> 00:01:36,083
Run as fast as you can and stop at the finish line.

39
00:01:36,083 --> 00:01:38,167
Remember to be careful.

40
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:40,417
All right, first group, get ready.

41
00:01:40,417 --> 00:01:40,833
Ready!

42
00:01:41,667 --> 00:01:42,917
Beep!

43
00:01:42,917 --> 00:01:44,917
And they’re off!

44
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,250
Go! Go! Go!

45
00:01:52,667 --> 00:01:53,167
Watch me!

46
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:55,500
I’m going to be as fast as a rocket!

47
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:59,917
I’ll fly across the sky, around the Earth,

48
00:01:59,917 --> 00:02:01,000
and all around the world!

49
00:02:03,417 --> 00:02:06,083
Haha! I made it! I knew I was the fastest!

50
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:09,333
Running is so much fun!

51
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:10,333
May!

52
00:02:10,333 --> 00:02:13,583
Y-you’re so fast! Are you a superhero?

53
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:16,667
Great job, everyone!

54
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:19,583
Especially May. You were practically flying!

55
00:02:19,833 --> 00:02:22,083
Second group, get ready.

56
00:02:22,083 --> 00:02:23,417
Ready!

57
00:02:27,667 --> 00:02:29,000
Beep!

58
00:02:29,917 --> 00:02:34,167
Go, go, go, Chuan-Chuan! Remember to use your imagination!

59
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:39,667
I’ll try my best! I can do it!

60
00:02:40,667 --> 00:02:41,167
I-I-I’m a locomotive!

61
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:43,167
I-I-I’m a locomotive!

62
00:02:44,167 --> 00:02:44,417
Choo-choo!

63
00:02:58,750 --> 00:02:59,667
I told you that you could do it!

64
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:02,583
Haha! Look at him!

65
00:03:02,583 --> 00:03:05,583
Chuan-Chuan runs so slowly, and his running looks so weird!

66
00:03:05,583 --> 00:03:06,750
Hahaha!

67
00:03:07,583 --> 00:03:09,500
What should I do?

68
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:14,417
Hey! Why are you laughing at him? You’re not that fast either!

69
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:16,833
You should focus on what others do well.

70
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,250
Bleh!

71
00:03:19,833 --> 00:03:22,000
All right, all right. Whether you’re fast or slow,

72
00:03:26,167 --> 00:03:28,417
you’ve all given your little muscles a good workout.

73
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:32,417
Don’t worry about it, Chuan-Chuan. You did great.

74
00:03:32,417 --> 00:03:35,083
Next is your favorite class: art!

75
00:03:35,083 --> 00:03:36,083
Let’s head back.

76
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:36,417
Mm-hmm.

77
00:03:36,583 --> 00:03:37,000
Mm-hmm.

78
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,500
May, thank you.

79
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:42,333
All right, children.

80
00:03:42,333 --> 00:03:43,917
Gym class is over.

81
00:03:43,917 --> 00:03:47,000
Now let’s draw “Everyone Exercising Together.”

82
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,583
Draw any kind of exercise you can think of.

83
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:53,583
Watch me! I have so many things to draw!

84
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:02,333
Whenever I draw at home, my mom and dad always encourage me.

85
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:03,917
They say my drawings are special.

86
00:04:05,583 --> 00:04:08,500
Look! This is what we looked like when we were running.

87
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:09,583
This is me.

88
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,833
This is Chuan-Chuan.

89
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:12,083
And these are you guys.

90
00:04:12,083 --> 00:04:14,083
Hmm, May…

91
00:04:14,083 --> 00:04:16,750
Your drawing really is unique.

92
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,333
Huh? May, what are you drawing?

93
00:04:19,333 --> 00:04:20,917
A plate of curry rice?

94
00:04:20,917 --> 00:04:22,333
I can’t tell what it is at all!

95
00:04:22,333 --> 00:04:23,167
Hahaha!

96
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,833
Pipi Monkey, you keep laughing at others.

97
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:31,917
Let’s see how good your drawing is.

98
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:41,000
I can’t tell what you’re drawing, either!

99
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:48,333
But Pipi Monkey used lots of different colors.

100
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:55,833
Everyone, come look! One child has made a particularly wonderful drawing.

101
00:04:57,333 --> 00:04:59,500
Chuan-Chuan, your drawing is great!

102
00:05:02,250 --> 00:05:04,583
Th-this is me. I love jumping rope!

103
00:05:05,083 --> 00:05:06,583
Mwah!

104
00:05:06,583 --> 00:05:09,667
That’s me running! Running is my favorite!

105
00:05:09,667 --> 00:05:12,333
That’s me! I love bouncing a ball!

106
00:05:12,333 --> 00:05:15,083
And I’m here! I love hanging from the monkey bars!

107
00:05:15,083 --> 00:05:17,250
Chuan-Chuan, you drew so well.

108
00:05:17,583 --> 00:05:20,583
I wish I could draw as well as you.

109
00:05:20,583 --> 00:05:24,833
I’m sorry. I shouldn’t have laughed at you when we were running.

110
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:29,333
That’s great, Chuan-Chuan. Just be yourself!

111
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:32,500
It’s okay.

112
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,333
Let’s draw together.

113
00:05:36,167 --> 00:05:38,333
Wonderful! You’re all doing great.

114
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:40,833
Everyone has things they’re good at and things they’re not so good at.

115
00:05:41,250 --> 00:05:44,333
What matters is appreciating other people’s strengths

116
00:05:44,333 --> 00:05:45,917
and respecting the ways they’re different.

117
00:05:45,917 --> 00:05:47,333
We’re all good friends!

118
00:05:47,333 --> 00:05:48,417
Class dismissed!

119
00:05:48,417 --> 00:05:52,750
Okay! Thank you, Teacher Capybara!
